Using another laptop, establish an SSH session to your Raspberry Pi from your terminal. 
Execute the official automated installation script.
Step through the interactive text installer.
Make sure to pick Google or Cloudflare as the DNS server.
Remember to save  the randomly generated Admin Web Password displayed at the final confirmation screen.
You are also going to be given an admin page for tracking.


Code
ssh pi@<yourraspberryipthatyoumade> (has to be static)
curl -sSL https://install.pi-hole.net | bash (this helps you install the Pi-hole service on your Pi)




